> expand (x+1)^3
  ucas: expand (x+1)^3
expand (x + 1)^3
  = x^3 + 3x^2 + 3x + 1
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor x^2 - 1
  ucas: factor x^2 - 1
factor x^2 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> simplify sin(x)^2 + cos(x)^2
  ucas: trig sin(x)^2 + cos(x)^2
  note: x is taken as real
trig forms of sin(x)^2 + cos(x)^2
  simplified: sin^2 + cos^2 = 1, cosh^2 - sinh^2 = 1, f(f^-1(u)) = u
    = 1
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
  simplest: 1  (simplified)
> together 1/x + 1/y
together 1/x + 1/y
  = (x + y)/(x*y)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> cancel (x^2-1)/(x-1)
cancel (x^2 - 1)/(x - 1)
  = x + 1
  holds where x - 1 != 0 (cancelled there)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> gcd x^2-1, x^2+2*x+1
gcd x^2 - 1, x^2 + 2x + 1
  = x + 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> diff x^3 + 2*x at x
  note: at is not a variable of x^3 + 2x: read as a product (for a derivative wrt at write `diff F wrt at`)
  note: 'at' read as a*t (single-letter variables)
  note: x^3 + 2(x*(a*t)*x) has 3 variables (x, a, t): all first partial derivatives, the gradient (say `diff F x` for one)
∇ x^3 + 2(x*(a*t)*x) = (3x^2 + 4x*a*t, 2x^2*t, 2x^2*a)
  ∂/∂x x^3 + 2(x*(a*t)*x) = 3x^2 + 4x*a*t
  ∂/∂a x^3 + 2(x*(a*t)*x) = 2x^2*t
  ∂/∂t x^3 + 2(x*(a*t)*x) = 2x^2*a
  holds wherever the formulas are defined
  check: every entry matches central differences at 300 points (max relative difference 8e-13)
> integrate x^2 from 0 to 1
∫ x^2 dx
  = x^3/3 + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 1] (max difference 1.1e-16)
  from 0 to 1: F(1) - F(0) = 0.333333333333333
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 0.333333333333333, estimated error 3.7e-15
  the two agree to 0
